{
  "title": "Quadratic Word Problems — Math Meets Real Life 🌍",
  "hook": "Two water pipes fill a pool. Working together they take 12 hours. Pipe A alone takes 10 hours more than Pipe B alone. How long does each pipe take? This is a real-life problem that leads to a quadratic equation!",
  "explanation": "The strategy for word problems:\n\n<div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#6A1B9A;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div>\n<div><strong>Read & Identify</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">What is unknown? Assign it a variable (let x = ...).</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#6A1B9A;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div>\n<div><strong>Translate to Math</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Convert the English sentences into an equation.</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#6A1B9A;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div>\n<div><strong>Solve the Quadratic</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Use factorization or the quadratic formula.</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#6A1B9A;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div>\n<div><strong>Check & Reject</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Reject negative or nonsensical answers (e.g., negative age, negative length).</span></div></div></div>\n<strong>Common Types:</strong>\n\n<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Type</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">What leads to x²</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Example Setup</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Area problems</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">length × width = area</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Rectangle: x(x+5) = 150</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Consecutive numbers</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">n × (n+1) = product</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">n(n+1) = 182</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Speed-Distance-Time</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Speed = Distance/Time</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">If speed ↑ by 5, time ↓ by 3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Age problems</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Present × Future age</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">(x)(x+4) = 192</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Work-Time</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/x + 1/y = 1/total</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/x + 1/(x+10) = 1/12</td></tr></table>\n<div style=\"background:#FFF3E0;border-left:4px solid #E65100;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">⚠️ <strong>Tip:</strong> Always check if both roots make sense in the original context! A length can't be negative, time can't be negative, and number of people must be a whole number.</div>",
  "worked_example": "<strong>The product of two consecutive positive integers is 306. Find them.</strong>\n\n<div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div>\n<div><strong>Let the integers be</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">x and x + 1</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div>\n<div><strong>Form the equation</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">x(x + 1) = 306<br>x² + x − 306 = 0</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div>\n<div><strong>Solve by factorization</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Find two numbers: sum = 1, product = −306<br>Numbers: 18 and −17<br>x² + 18x − 17x − 306 = 0<br>x(x + 18) − 17(x + 18) = 0<br>(x − 17)(x + 18) = 0</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div>\n<div><strong>Find x</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">x = 17 or x = −18</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">5</div>\n<div><strong>Reject & Conclude</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Since integers are positive, x = 17.<br><strong>The integers are 17 and 18.</strong> ✓ (17 × 18 = 306 ✓)</span></div></div></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "The altitude of a right triangle is 7 cm less than its base. If the hypotenuse is 13 cm, find the other two sides.",
    "hint": "Let base = x, altitude = x − 7. Use Pythagoras: x² + (x−7)² = 13².",
    "answer": "x² + (x−7)² = 169\nx² + x² − 14x + 49 = 169\n2x² − 14x − 120 = 0\nx² − 7x − 60 = 0\n(x − 12)(x + 5) = 0\nx = 12 (reject −5)\nBase = 12 cm, Altitude = 5 cm.\nCheck: 12² + 5² = 144 + 25 = 169 = 13² ✓"
